---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Josh J Wilkinson and this site — who keeps it, and why it is built the way it is."
>
  <article class="about measure">
    <header class="about__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <section class="contact-card" aria-labelledby="contact-name">
        <h1 id="contact-name">Joshua Wilkinson</h1>
        <address>
          <a href="mailto:joshjeffreywilkinson@gmail.com">joshjeffreywilkinson@gmail.com</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jjwilkin" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            linkedin.com/in/jjwilkin
          </a>
        </address>
      </section>
    </header>

    <div class="prose flow">
      <p class="lead">
        I build systems — databases, distributed machinery, and the unglamorous plumbing that
        keeps software upright under load. This is where I keep notes on that work and the ideas
        that escape its boundaries.
      </p>

      <p>
        I made this because the usual containers never quite fit. A portfolio flattens a person
        into deliverables; a feed makes everything equally disposable. I wanted a quieter place
        for essays, technical notes, photographs, and unfinished observations.
      </p>

      <p>
        Posts appear chronologically on the homepage and collect naturally under
        <a href="/tags/">tags</a>. The structure stays deliberately small so the writing remains the
        main event.
      </p>

      <h2>How to read it</h2>
      <p>
        Wander, don't sprint. Start with the latest piece or choose a tag and move sideways. Once
        you're reading, everything else gets out of the way; longer pieces are set for comfort,
        not for show.
      </p>

      <h2>Colophon</h2>
      <p>
        Text is set in <span class="u-ui">Spectral</span>, with
        <span class="u-ui">IBM Plex Mono</span> for navigation and metadata. The blue-and-white
        palette borrows from qinghua porcelain. The site is built with
        <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and published as static files so it stays fast and
        durable.
      </p>

    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-top: 44px;
  }
  .about__head {
    margin-bottom: 38px;
  }

  .about__head > .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .contact-card {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    aspect-ratio: 1.8 / 1;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    align-items: end;
    gap: 30px;
    padding: clamp(30px, 5vw, 42px);
    border: 1px solid var(--blue);
    background-color: var(--paper);
    background-image: var(--paper-grain);
    background-repeat: repeat;
    background-size: 180px 180px;
  }

  .contact-card::after {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 5px;
    border: 1px solid var(--blue-pale);
    content: '';
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .contact-card h1 {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: none;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 44px);
    line-height: 0.98;
    overflow-wrap: normal;
  }

  .contact-card address {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 7px;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 10px;
    font-style: normal;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .contact-card a {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .about :global(.prose) {
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .about {
      padding-top: 30px;
    }

    .about__head {
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }

    .contact-card {
      aspect-ratio: 1.55 / 1;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      align-content: space-between;
      align-items: start;
      gap: 26px;
      padding: 28px;
    }

    .contact-card h1 {
      font-size: 38px;
    }

    .contact-card address {
      font-size: 9px;
    }
  }
</style>
